{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And YHWH went before them by day</b> The Sages have already said (Bereshit Rabbah 51:2) that wherever <b>וַה'</b> (\"and YHWH\") is stated, it means He and His heavenly court — the Holy One, blessed be He, with them by day, and His heavenly court by night. If so, the meaning of the verse is that HaShem dwells within the cloud and He Himself goes before them by day in a pillar of cloud, and at night His heavenly court dwells in the pillar of fire to give them light, in the sense of \"in whose eyes You are seen face to face, YHWH, and Your cloud stands over them, and in a pillar of cloud You go before them by day and in a pillar of fire by night\" (Numbers 14:14). <b>And I saw</b> in Shemot Rabbah (19:6) on \"For you shall not go out in haste, nor flee in flight, for YHWH goes before you\" (Isaiah 52:12) — in the past, I and My heavenly court went before you, as it is said, <b>and YHWH went before them by day</b>, but in the time to come I alone, as it is said (Isaiah 52:12), \"for YHWH goes before you and the God of Israel is your rear guard.\" And the secret of this midrash is as I have mentioned, that in the first redemption the Holy One, blessed be He, was with them by day and His heavenly court with them by night, but in the time to come the attribute of justice will be subsumed within mercy — <b>and YHWH goes before them</b>, the singular Name, for the God of Israel gathers them with Him, and night as day will give light, darkness as light (Psalms 139:12), for everything is unified in the attribute of mercy. And R. Abraham [Ibn Ezra] said (on Exodus 13:21) that Scripture speaks in human language, because the power of HaShem and His emissary is what goes with Israel, in the manner of \"who leads them at the right hand of Moses, the arm of His glory\" (Isaiah 63:12). The truth is that it is in the manner of \"who leads them at the right hand of Moses,\" but not in the way that R. Abraham understands it from the verse, as it is written, \"So You guided Your people, to make for Yourself a name of glory\" (Isaiah 63:14)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {0 "Reading הקב\"ה throughout as 'the Holy One, blessed be He,' following the standard expansion of this reverent abbreviation."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:07:39.748051115Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}